## Context

T0104 shipped first-class **ToDo** records (`D####`) with state/priority/due/actionBy and editor tags. To Do **list view** (`TodoListView`) is still a flat checklist: membership DnD exists; no filter bar, no row tag chips, no inline priority/due.

Task List View (`TasksListPage` / `TaskBoard` + `TaskListFilterBar` / `taskListFilter.ts`) is the reuse target. T0097 (hierarchy) is still Ready — not shipped → **flat** reorder only.

## Goals / acceptance

1. **Tags in list** — `RowTagChips` on ToDo and Task rows (same patterns as Task list).
2. **Filters** — compound filter bar comparable to Task List: at least tags, priority, due date, state; persist per list.
3. **Inline fields** — priority and due date editable on the row without opening the modal (ToDo → `PATCH /todos/:id`; Task → `PATCH /tasks/:id`).
4. **DnD** — keep existing list-item reorder; when filters hide rows, reorder among **visible** membership and stitch into full order (TaskBoard-style). No hierarchy/chains until T0097.

## Out of scope

- Due-date presets (T0099), recurrence (T0100), row tinting (T0102), extra action fields (T0101)
- ToDo record type / schema (T0104 done)
- Nested ToDos / completion rollup (T0097)
- New Drizzle migration (tags already polymorphic for `todo`)

## Recommended approach

### 1. Filter model + persistence

- Add a thin To Do list filter module (or generalize `taskListFilter` with a field set for list scope):
  - Fields: **state**, **priority**, **dueDate** (and/or relative due buckets if cheap), **tags**, **title**, **checked** (list item), optionally **entityType** (`todo` | `task`)
  - Drop Task-only: **phase**, **project** (list already scoped); keep title search for triage
- Reuse `TaskListFilterBar` UI with a field-list prop / scope, or a `TodoListFilterBar` wrapper sharing styles
- Persist: `taskmesh.todoListFilter.list:{listId}` via hook patterned on `usePersistedTaskListFilter`
- Evaluate client-side over hydrated list items (+ taggings loaded for visible entities)

### 2. Tags on rows

- Load taggings for items in the list (batch or existing tag lookup hooks)
- Render `RowTagChips` for `entityType` `todo` | `task`
- Tag filter clauses match either entity type’s tags

### 3. Inline state / priority / due

- Compact row controls: state `<select>` (Draft, Ready, In Progress, Complete, Canceled, On Hold), priority `<select>`, due `<input type="date">`
- Patch correct API by `item.entityType`; refresh list hydration on success
- List checkbox (`checked`) remains separate from entity state

### 4. DnD polish

- Keep `@dnd-kit` membership reorder → `PATCH …/items/reorder`
- When filter is active: DnD among **visible** rows; stitch into full membership order (`reorderVisibleAmongAll`)
- No entity-level `todos.sortOrder` reorder API in this Task

### 5. Surface priority / state on compact row

- Inline controls replace muted text cues so triage works without expanding

## Implementation sketch (files)

- `client/src/components/TodoListView.tsx` — filter bar, chips, inline state/priority/due, DnD on filtered visible rows
- New: `client/src/lib/todoListFilter.ts`, `usePersistedTodoListFilter.ts`, `TodoListFilterBar.tsx` (or shared bar with field set)
- Due presets: Today = calendar day; Soon = today through +2 days (3-day window); This Week = calendar week (Mon–Sun); This Month = calendar month. BEFORE/AFTER use window start/end.
- Reuse: `RowTagChips.tsx`; taggings for `todo` + `task` in filter context
- API: client-side filter only; PATCH todos/tasks for inline fields

## QA follow-ups

- **Row layout** — ToDo list rows used flex + global `select`/`date` `width: 100%`, so State/Priority/Due stacked vertically. Switched `.todo-item` to a Task-like CSS grid so fields stay on one compact row.
- **Tag chips** — same implementation as Task list: `RowTagChips` inside the title cell (title text · chips · State). Shared `.row-tag-chips` only; spacing via `margin-right: 20px` (not padding inside `overflow: hidden`, which clipped pill corners).
- **Idea modal Description** — T0104 had stripped the To Do list Idea modal to read-only title + tags. Restored editable Title + Description (`MarkdownEditor` on `body`) + tags, keeping the legacy convert note.

